            <ArticleTitle>[Echoccardiographic hyperventilation test in patients with negative coronarography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Opportunities to examine patients with spastic angina pectoris are at present, due to the inaccessibility of ergonovine, very limited. The authors demonstrate on a small group of patients the application of echocardiographic hyperventilation test for assessment of the diagnosis of spastic angina pectoris.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
